      "expect": {
        "exit": 0,
        "stdout": "",
        "stderr": "1: Bad file descriptor\nrc=1\ne=1\n"
      },
      "note": "bash 5.2: a self-dup is a no-op, so a descriptor closed earlier on the line stays closed and the later dup from it is refused before the command runs."
